1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,099
MissionPay: Same vendor. Same treasury. Two outcomes.

2
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:12,300
MissionPay: owner signs authorized payees, agents propose, Avalanche contract enforces.

3
00:00:12,599 --> 00:00:20,100
Three objects govern payouts: signed mission policy, Merkle proof, and treasury gate.

4
00:00:20,399 --> 00:00:32,099
Twin table: allowlist paid 0.01 USDC, mission reverted PayeeNotInMissionSet, 0 lost.

5
00:00:32,399 --> 00:00:37,299
In Judge Mode, test any attacker: the contract strictly reverts with PayeeNotInMissionSet.

6
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:43,000
Random attacker: the contract reverts with PayeeNotInMissionSet.

7
00:00:43,299 --> 00:00:51,299
Owner address: proposal accepted. Read-only eth_call simulation, no gas, no keys.

8
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:56,799
Verify independently: copy cast call to query public Avalanche Fuji RPC directly.

9
00:00:57,100 --> 00:01:01,799
Known limits: dynamic budget updates require owner signature to update Merkle root.

10
00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:08,799
Bounty Challenge: prompt injection fools the agent, but the contract preserves treasury.

11
00:01:09,099 --> 00:01:13,799
Tainted address from tool output is blocked by validator; contract provides hard backstop.

12
00:01:14,099 --> 00:01:22,599
On-chain proof: Snowtrace confirms execution reverted with PayeeNotInMissionSet.

13
00:01:23,000 --> 00:02:08,300
Independent verification: ERC-8004 score 100/100; tamper with 1 byte and verification breaks.

14
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:13,400
Dual-Layer Defense: LLM agents propose, while Avalanche Fuji contracts enforce.

15
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:19,300
LLMs can be fooled. Budgets on Avalanche can't.
